from pathlib import Path
p=Path('docs/V20_STARTUP_AUDIT.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('# V20 startup and drive state-machine audit\n', '# V20 startup and drive state-machine audit\n\n> **Development update:** Sections 1–15 preserve the original read-only baseline. See section 16 for the implemented corrections, current bench configuration, validation results and outstanding installation checks. Baseline line numbers and flag values describe the audited revision, not the updated files.\n',1);p.write_text(s)
p=Path('ESP32/README.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Hardware permissions remain disabled until explicitly validated. Do not override commissioning gates to test the fan.', 'The operator has requested a bench release with the motor disconnected: safety I/O, V20 command and frequency-model permission flags are enabled, while torque AUTO is disabled. This is not installation validation; physical interlocks and deliberate RESET/START remain mandatory. See the current implementation matrix in [the V20 audit](../docs/V20_STARTUP_AUDIT.md#16-implementation-and-validation-update).');s=s.replace('`INIT → WAIT → READY → RUNNING → STOP → FAULT`','`INIT → WAIT → STOPPED_PREPARE → READY → STARTING → RUNNING → STOP → READY` (with latched FAULT branches)');s=s.replace('`SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED` remains disabled.', '`SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED=1` is the requested motor-disconnected bench setting, not a measured validation record.');s=s.replace('`CONTROL_TYPE=CONTROL_TORQUE_PI` (default) or `CONTROL_FREQUENCY_PI`','`CONTROL_TYPE=CONTROL_FREQUENCY_PI` (current default) or `CONTROL_TORQUE_PI`');s=s.replace('Frequency defaults have no approved identified model and remain inhibited until validation/commissioning.', 'Frequency permission flags are enabled by operator request; numeric identification defaults (gain and time constant) remain zero and valid stored fan calibration is still required. No model values are invented; AUTO start reports CONFIGURATION if these prerequisites are missing.');s=s.replace('`SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED=0` and `V20_RUN_COMMISSIONED=0` are also documented as uncommissioned defaults.', '`SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED=1` and `V20_RUN_COMMISSIONED=1` are the requested bench settings.');p.write_text(s)
p=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text().replace('`SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED=0`, `V20_RUN_COMMISSIONED=0` and `MOTOR_MODEL_TORQUE_TO_V20_ENABLED=0` are documented uncommissioned settings; verify the actual build configuration.', 'Current motor-disconnected bench configuration (operator request): `SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED=1`, `V20_RUN_COMMISSIONED=1`, frequency-model permissions enabled and selected, `MOTOR_MODEL_TORQUE_TO_V20_ENABLED=0`. This does not validate the installation, numeric frequency identification or fan calibration. See [current V20 audit](docs/V20_STARTUP_AUDIT.md#16-implementation-and-validation-update).');p.write_text(s)
p=Path('docs/hardware/V20_MODBUS.md');s=p.read_text().replace('| Watchdog | 40001 | 0 | 500 ms |','| Watchdog | 40001 | 0 | Readback only; not assumed identical to P2014 |');s=s.replace('The driver uses FC16 for combined STW/HSW writes, FC03 for reads and FC06 for watchdog configuration.', 'The driver uses FC16 for combined STW/HSW writes and FC03 for reads. It does not configure the watchdog or automatically change V20 parameters.');s=s.replace('Driver initialization requests OFF1 and checks the reference and status before permitting operation.', 'Driver initialization bootstraps with status/reference/watchdog reads and then requests OFF1 when V20 writes are permitted. STOPPED_PREPARE verifies a post-reset stopped command and fresh stopped feedback before READY; STARTING waits for post-START operation-enabled feedback.');s=s.replace('- **AUTO:** Pitot airspeed feedback, a fifth-order reference, one-mass torque PID and an approximate inverse motor model that generates V20 frequency.\n- There is **no separate legacy frequency-domain PI controller** in the current firmware.\n- Real AUTO remains inhibited until motor and fan model parameters are independently validated.', '- **AUTO:** selectable identified frequency PI (current selection) or torque PID/inverse model. Both share physical START and safety handling.\n- Frequency permissions are enabled for the requested motor-disconnected bench configuration; numeric identification and valid calibration are still checked. Torque-to-V20 remains disabled.\n- None of these settings prove physical commissioning.');p.write_text(s)
p=Path('docs/hardware/MACHINE-IO.md');s=p.read_text().replace('| Yellow lamp | DO3 | Bit 2 | Proposed INIT / WAIT / STOP indication |','| Red lamp | DO3 | Bit 2 | Current firmware FAULT indication; verify installed wiring |').replace('| Red lamp | DO4 | Bit 3 | Proposed FAULT / emergency indication |','| Yellow lamp | DO4 | Bit 3 | Current firmware INIT / WAIT / PREPARE / STARTING / STOP indication; verify installed wiring |');s=s.replace('SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED and V20_RUN_COMMISSIONED remain 0. Do not enable these flags\nuntil the corresponding installation has been verified independently.', 'SAFETY_IO_COMMISSIONED and V20_RUN_COMMISSIONED are now 1 by explicit operator request for the motor-disconnected bench setup. This does not establish independent installation verification. DO1 supplies the intended V20 In1/OFF2 permission after RESET and an acknowledged OFF1 in STOPPED_PREPARE, and stays enabled in healthy READY/STARTING/RUNNING/STOP. Live safety gates remain mandatory. See the updated V20 audit for outstanding as-built checks.');p.write_text(s)
